# Build-context exclusions for EVERY image build (the compose-native installer, the Semaphore runner, the Vector
# image). The installer image (docker/installer/Dockerfile) does `COPY . /repo`; without this, the dev node's
# live `instance/` overlay (the age private key, the SOPS recipients, the real-IP inventory, instance/trust) and
# `local/` ssh keys would bake into an image layer. The compose-native security floor forbids any secret in an
# image (synthesis §5); tests/unit/test_installer_phase1.py pins these exclusions so they can't silently regress.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's secret patterns. KEEP ansible/collections/*.generated.yml — gitignored, but the Semaphore
# runner image bakes the fleet collections from it (docker/semaphore-runner/Dockerfile). Do NOT add a
# *.generated.* exclude here.

# Private instance overlay (age key, SOPS secrets, .sops.yaml recipients, real-IP inventory, trust root) + scratch
instance/
local/

# age private keys + decrypted secret outputs (mirror .gitignore)
*.agekey
keys.txt
**/sops/age/keys.txt
*.dec
*.decrypted
*.plain.yml
*.plain.yaml

# Runtime env files (rendered with secrets; host bind, never an image layer)
.env
**/.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Not needed in any image; large or noise
.git/
.github/
docs/reviews/
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.retry
